From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: detect macOS output speakers and route up to eight PCM channels

Snapshot the selected/default output's configured speaker layout when the guest
first reads device config. Advertise fixed mono-to-eight-channel PCM maps in ALSA
order, retaining explicitly identified height speakers. Do not infer 5.1.2 from
an eight-channel count: unclassified/discrete layouts use the preferred stereo
pair. Capture remains mono/stereo. Correct config.chmaps to match all entries.

Use a device-bound HAL output unit and recheck the default/selected device and
layout once a second. The callback consumes guest-format PCM on the existing
ring/clock, then applies a precomputed speaker matrix into interleaved Float32
physical outputs. Missing speakers fold into front channels with headroom;
unknown physical channels stay silent. Rebuild/retry output units on hotplug
without changing guest frame accounting or allocating/locking in the callback.
The WAV diagnostic now captures guest PCM before mapping.

Guest maps remain fixed for a boot: virtio-snd/ALSA cache PCM capabilities and
there is no PCM-info/channel-map-change event. Restart the VM to expose added
channels or a new guest speaker layout. This is PCM routing, not Atmos encoding.

Validation: cargo check -p krun-devices --features snd; cargo test -p
krun-devices --features snd --test macos_audio (11 tests). HAL Float32 format,
identity channel map and initialization also checked on an eight-channel Mac
output. Physical speaker listening and live device-switch tests remain.
